WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:08.400
Constellatory Dreams

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.160
The Netherlands is known for its wooden clogs

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.160
and its yummy cheese!

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.080
Looks like the next one will be somewhere around here.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.200
Yeah.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.810
Following their recent raid in Russia,

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:46.150
the Blue Hawk gang has also captured stockpiles of methane hydrate in the Netherlands...

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.520
That incident is currently under investigation.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.570
Considering that the raid occurred shortly after your statement

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.530
about providing a stable source of energy,

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.960
suspicion toward the Adnimoon Company is mounting worldwide—

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.410
Regarding that incident...

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.700
An obligatory audit of our own security systems will be performed.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.540
We will also request that the local police be involved in all security matters

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.050
in order to ensure that these thieves are brought to justice.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.610
An eye for an eye.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:23.890
"Until now, I had never felt any need to be understood.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.330
"I had never felt lonely...

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:30.560
"Not until I met you."

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:52.590
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:52.590
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:00.390
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:00.390
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.640
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.640
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.730
shinkuromanika

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.730
Synchromanica

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.270
itsu no ma ni ka

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.270
Before I know it

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.440
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.440
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:20.740
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:20.740
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:27.250
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:27.250
I can hear someone's dream

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:34.210
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:34.210
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.020
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.020
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.350
shinkuromanika

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.350
Synchromanica

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.480
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.480
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.520
shinkuromanika

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.520
Synchromanica

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.740
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.740
The synchrony of your life

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.060
It's colder than I'd expected.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.300
Well, that's one of the first signs of an ice age.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.140
Our next stop is the church, right?

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:28.440
Let's find it quickly.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.640
Okay.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.690
Is this some kind of ghost town?

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.650
I don't see any sign of a church.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.360
According to the map, it should be around here.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.150
Freeze!

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.050
What?

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:50.160
W-We're just tourists from Italy!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.660
Enough with the lame excuses.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.920
You're those wanted Ferrari sisters, aren't you?

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.210
I'm Ludger Verhoeven, the Blue Hawk's leader.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.180
The Blue Hawk... You mean the ring of thieves?

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.930
As fellow refugees from the law,
we welcome you on your visit here.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.520
We aren't anything like you guys!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.170
Besides, why are you pointing guns in our faces?

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.770
Hazuki-chan, calm down.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.650
Lower your guns.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:22.030
We just came by to do some shopping...

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.780
Although, I don't see any stores here.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.780
Yeah.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:30.330
The railroad was shut down a while ago, and this is all that's left of the village.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.830
It's too cold to talk out here.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.710
Let me get you some hot chocolate.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:37.990
Follow me.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:48.550
The Adnimoon Company's business practices are pretty low, don't you think?

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:53.520
They only expand into large cities or other areas already full of wealthy people.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.060
They've used the energy shortage

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.450
as an excuse to cut off power to smaller, more rural villages.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.570
It's pretty unfair.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.070
How are things where you're from?

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.780
I can't think of any serious hardships.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.040
Then you guys had it pretty good.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.700
We were careful to conserve.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:17.850
Everybody here, myself included, has had a similar experience.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.240
We had no choice but to abandon our hometowns.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:26.300
After a while, the people the Adnimoon Company had wronged began to band together.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.720
And eventually we were branded as a ring of thieves.

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.220
All the same, stealing is stealing.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.100
Don't be that way.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.770
There are 30 of us in total.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.850
We're just one big family, you know?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.560
We manage to make it work, though.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.480
Even if it's just to keep the cold and hunger at bay.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.990
The Adnimoon Company is evil.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:50.840
Having your energy supply cut off doesn't just threaten your livelihood.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:53.130
It gets to you mentally, as well.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.870
Girls, those people would even take away what happiness we have here.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.580
If nothing changes, soon we won't even have lives to live.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:03.390
Regardless, attacking transport ships won't solve your problems!

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.680
You should be going through the official channels

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.920
and lodging a complaint against the
Adnimoon Company, don't you think?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.010
Yours are the words of the privileged.

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:17.020
I already told you. We've been cut off.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.000
We can protest all we want,
but our pleas will fall on deaf ears.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.860
We neither have, nor can we afford, the time—

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.740
Excuse me!

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.990
May I use the restroom?

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.200
So cold!

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:38.520
Hey...

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.500
Huh?

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:45.440
That unusual goldfish-looking thing that you guys came in on...

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:46.820
Where's it from?

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.300
Actually, I made it.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.050
<i>You</i> did?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.910
<i>You</i> made this?

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.850
Wow, this really is amazing.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.690
You might just be a genius.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.360
I'm not that smart...

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.930
You're the next smartest after me!

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:15.370
I'm Theo Escher.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.370
I'm Hozuki Ferrari.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.360
Nice to meet you.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:22.880
What's this thing?

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.300
Hozuki-chan brought a boy on board!

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.300
Grande Rosso, an AI.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:29.670
Whoa, awesome.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.800
Do you also build fish, Theo?

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:37.120
No. To do that kind of thing you need a certain environment and the right components.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:43.560
But in my head, I'm building things way bigger than this!

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:49.920
Next year, Ludger's gonna make it so that I can go study at a school.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.320
I'll be able to build a real fish after that, though!

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.560
Until then, I'm gonna do my best to help everybody here.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.580
You've really thought it through, huh?

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:04.500
If you have tech like this,

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.120
I bet you could do a lot for the world, too.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:09.420
Okay!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.920
Next, it's my turn!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:12.770
What?

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.730
Call it what you like, but stealing won't...

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:15.430
Man...

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.110
I guess they fired up Hazu-nee's sense of justice.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:24.140
I didn't know the energy problem was quite this bad.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:28.070
And the further north we went,
the more the temperature dropped.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.230
You're kidding, right?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.610
It's been all over the news.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.280
Is the goldfish doing okay for fuel?

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:36.910
That's right...

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.990
We need to find that sketch as soon as possible.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:45.210
Kazuki-chan, let's look for the church tomorrow as soon as the sun is up.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.750
Huh? Me?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.420
Didn't you want to get home soon?

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.350
We aren't hogging the energy!

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.940
Well, yeah...

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.840
If we do nothing, hundreds—No, thousands will die!

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:55.840
Wow...

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.720
You made this telescope?

00:08:58.720 --> 00:08:59.850
Well, yeah.

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.770
It's amazing.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.310
What're you talking about?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.850
You could make something like this easily, right?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:10.320
Whenever I've built anything,
I've never had to make do with scrap material.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.540
It's easy.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:14.400
When I still went to school,

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.740
I actually found a blueprint for
Galileo's telescope in the library.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.210
So I modeled it after that one.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.290
I see.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.370
You're lucky, you know.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.790
I just finished this yesterday.

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:27.960
"To Karen"?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.000
Galileo built a telescope with a 20x magnification

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.800
and looked at the Moon.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:38.730
He, with his own eyes, discovered that the Moon's surface is riddled with craters.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:40.960
From there, he made his Moon sketches.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:43.480
You know, Galileo once said:

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:49.190
"All truths are easy to understand once they are discovered;

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.630
the point is to discover them."

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.780
You're the first person I've met that I can talk to like this.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.280
Same here.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.700
Theo?

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:05.830
What?

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.470
It's dinnertime.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.470
I'll be right there.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.660
Who is she?

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:15.590
Karen.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.470
We've known each other forever.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.140
Theo—

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.140
Theo.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:30.650
Hmm?

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:33.320
Put the gun away when you're eating.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.730
It's distasteful.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:35.520
Ludger!

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.940
Please take me with you on your next job!

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.730
I want to help everyone!

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.910
Okay, I'll consider it.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.080
All right!

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.920
It's so nice that you can understand what Theo talks about.

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:06.720
Huh?

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:11.520
It's too hard for me to understand, so it all sounds like gibberish.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.940
I think we just happen to have the same hobby.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:19.950
It's nice when you can enjoy the same things as other people, isn't it?

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:24.140
Theo always calls me an idiot.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:26.240
I don't think he likes me.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.120
I—I don't think it's like that...

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:35.360
Hey, do you like Theo?

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.170
I knew it!

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:42.380
Hey, is it your birthday today?

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:46.970
Yeah... How did you know?

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:51.750
Oh, um... It was just a hunch.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:12:01.700
"Until now, I had never felt any need to be understood.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:05.450
"I had never felt lonely...

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.930
"Not until I met you."

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:09.900
What's that?

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:11.940
Is there someone you like, too?

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.960
No, I didn't write that.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.370
Well?

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.330
This map is really old.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:24.130
We're going to have to find it on foot.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.090
Thanks, Hozuki-chan.

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:34.330
Don't mention it.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.060
Welcome back.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.570
I'm back, Theo.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.810
Y-You know... I have something I wanna give to you.

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.070
Later!

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.320
Is everything okay?

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:51.580
Yeah, I'll see her later, anyway.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.330
But anyway, take a look at this.
I've made some adjustments.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.210
A new lens?

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.040
I'm surprised you found one.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:58.920
Yeah.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.250
I kind of "borrowed" it from the church.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.440
Church?

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.170
Where is it?!

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:07.290
Uh, it's right here.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.510
It was remodeled into a train station.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:12.780
Oh, so it's here.

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:14.020
What's here?

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:17.620
Sorry I didn't tell you earlier,

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:21.860
but I'm actually looking for Galileo's Moon sketches.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.180
Sketches?

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.340
Yeah.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:26.030
And...

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:30.510
Galileo Galilei happens to be my ancestor.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.770
What?!

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.790
They totally changed things...

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:42.320
A goldfish!

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:48.390
Hey, what is it?

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:52.220
Hey, wait!

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.070
Did you figure something out?

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.730
There it is!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.250
A fish?

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.130
Could you help me check this out?

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:02.980
S-Sure.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.250
So the entire floor was a sundial...

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.250
Yeah.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:25.260
There was so much trash on it, I never noticed.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:45.330
So this is a real Moon sketch?

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.610
Yeah.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.610
Um, can I show this to Ludger?

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:55.290
I mean, who would've guessed that something this amazing was right beneath us?

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.790
Even Ludger would be amazed!

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:02.420
But I'd like to take it with me.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.930
Wouldn't he be opposed to that?

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:06.250
It'll be fine.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.800
He's a very generous man.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:14.680
If it'll help you find what you're looking for, I think he'll be happy to let you take it.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.310
Okay, got it.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.730
Indeed. That's correct.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:25.200
Roger.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:33.720
It doesn't seem to be around here.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.620
Let's head back for now.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.620
Where are Hazu-nee and Hocchibi?

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.630
I'm here.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:46.410
Whoa, what's with that getup?

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.630
I think I caught a cold.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.840
The Galileo Tesoro, huh?

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:55.140
Yeah, the sketches contain clues to solve the mystery.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.600
Ludger!

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.610
We found something unbelievable
in the train station's basement!

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.800
Take a guess!

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:08.570
What?

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:11.760
We found a Galileo Moon sketch!

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:12.520
And—

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:13.150
Theo!

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:15.660
I'm sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:17.360
Where are you going?

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:25.170
Enemy assault! Enemy assault!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.090
Aza Irons incoming at high speed!

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:30.960
Where's Hocchii?

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.930
Theo!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:33.880
Theo?

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:41.890
Ludger!

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.560
I'll go call for help!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.490
Stop!

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.820
We aren't going to intercept them.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:50.170
I can't fight them.

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:52.530
What are you talking about?

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.950
Don't think too poorly of me.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.320
What the hell's going on, Ludger?

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:02.480
You're the one who said that we have to take a stand against Adnimoon!

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:06.220
I've thought long and hard about our options...

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:09.590
But there's nothing more that I can do.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:13.360
You guys had best run while you still can, too.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.670
They're going to bomb this place soon.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:18.780
No way...

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:21.370
Ludger, you sold us out?

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:24.730
Theo, get out of the way.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:25.560
No!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.000
Damn it!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.170
Damn you, Ludger!

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.050
One mini-fish just left the tunnel.

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:05.020
It's that boy.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.750
Hey, Hozuki!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:13.860
Are you okay?

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.860
The <i>Galileo</i>'s here, looking for you.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.730
Hurry up and get out of here!

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:21.120
What about you?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:23.530
I have to protect Karen.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:27.120
Talking with you was a lot of fun.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.120
I hope we'll see each other again someday!

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:31.380
Theo!

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:44.770
Hozuki-chan!

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:44.770
Hocchibi!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:45.950
Anna-san!

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:49.980
They've started bombing...

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:51.370
Hozuki-chan, hurry!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:55.610
Anna-san, please, we have to save Theo and the others, too!

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:04.620
Karen!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.530
What the hell are you doing here?

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:10.220
Theo!

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:12.340
Why didn't you run with everyone else?

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.560
This is your beloved telescope!

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:18.270
I was planning to give it to you...

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.260
Don't tell me you waited for me because of that?

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:27.320
Theo, you remembered my birthday.

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:28.430
Thanks!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.330
Can you stand, Karen?

00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:45.410
The telescope...

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.690
I can just make another one!

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:57.360
Karen, you...

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.070
I'm sorry.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.200
Stop, Hocchibi!

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:28.690
I'm going to save Theo!

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:29.700
I'm gonna save him!

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.700
We'll never make it in time!

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.730
We won't!

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:35.710
Changing pilot.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.370
The <i>Galileo</i> is going to retreat.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:39.460
Grande Rosso?

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:41.120
If we don't retreat,

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:46.290
the probability that we will be shot down by the Aza Irons is 99.8%.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
